  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri I. Kondala Rao vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 4 September, 2020",
    "facts": "Then the police caught hoid of the said person and asked about the details and A-3 confessed that he used to supply tobacco products from like Gutkha, Khainee etc., to all kirana shops and used to buy tobacco products from the petitioner / A-1 and other accused. Basing on the confessional statement of A-3, the police registered a crime and added the petitioner as Accused No.1.",
    "arguments": "The learned counsel for the petitioner submits that in respect of other crimes under IPC, COTP Act and FSS Act, this Court has already [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings in FIR No.588 of 2020 vide order dated 22.07.2020 in Crl.P.No.2767 of 2020. Learned counsel further submits that only basing on the confessional statement of A-3, the petitioner/A-1 was implicated in the crime, except that, there is no material to show that the petitioner/A-1 was involved in the crime. The learned counsel submits that only 4 KGs of ganja is seized from A-3 which is not a commercial quantity.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The learned counsel for the petitioner submits that in respect of other crimes under IPC, COTP Act and FSS Act, this Court has already [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings in FIR No.588 of 2020 vide order dated 22.07.2020 in Crl.P.No.2767 of 2020. Learned counsel further submits that only basing on the confessional statement of A-3, the petitioner/A-1 was implicated in the crime, except that, there is no material to show that the petitioner/A-1 was involved in the crime. The learned counsel submits that only 4 KGs of ganja is seized from A-3 which is not a commercial quantity.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
